INT. MOBILE SURGICAL TRUCK, FAIRGROUND - NIGHT

Steel walls. Fluorescent hum. Outside, a carousel plays a warped waltz.

DR. IMELDA CASTELLANOS-BRIGHT (50s, silver braid, precise) scrubs at a stainless sink. Across the narrow room, ANTON "TOOTS" VASSILIEV (30s, medic, tattooed forearms) wheels in a gurney. A sheet covers the shape on it.

IMELDA
Toots. Slower.

TOOTS
Sorry, Doc. Floor's uneven.

IMELDA
It's a truck in a field. Everything's uneven.

Toots locks the gurney. The carousel music thins, then swells.

TOOTS
Vitals are stable. Pressure's low, but he's talking.

IMELDA
Who is he?

TOOTS
Calls himself Wendell. Fell off the Ferris wheel.

IMELDA
Fell.

TOOTS
That's his word.

Imelda dries her hands. She folds the sheet back. WENDELL (60s, pale, cheerful, fairground jacket) squints up at the lights.

WENDELL
Hello, hello. Don't go to any trouble.

IMELDA
Mr. Wendell, I'm Dr. Castellanos-Bright. Where does it hurt?

WENDELL
Nowhere, really. Funny that.

IMELDA
(to Toots)
Pain meds?

TOOTS
None. He refused.

IMELDA
Refused?

WENDELL
I like to feel where I am.

She checks his pupils. He follows her light with unnerving ease. Toots shifts on his feet.

TOOTS
Doc, a word?

IMELDA
Say it here.

TOOTS
It's not a thing for here.

She holds his gaze. Then she walks him to the corner, out of Wendell's earshot.

IMELDA
(low)
What.

TOOTS
Fall was sixty feet. He landed on concrete.

IMELDA
And?

TOOTS
Nothing's broken. Not a rib. Not a bruise.

Imelda looks back at Wendell. He waves.

IMELDA
Then he's lucky.

TOOTS
Doc, I felt for a pulse four times. I couldn't find one.

The radio on the wall CRACKLES.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Mobile Two, dispatch. Ambulance en route, ETA fifteen. Say your patient's condition.

Imelda keys the radio, eyes on Wendell.

IMELDA
(into radio)
Dispatch, patient is stable. Repeat, stable.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(over radio)
Copy. Be advised, caller says the Ferris wheel victim was pronounced at the scene. Please confirm identity.

Silence. The carousel waltz winds down to a single note.

TOOTS
Doc.

IMELDA
I heard.

She turns. Wendell is sitting up, the sheet pooled at his waist. He's still smiling. His chest does not rise or fall.

WENDELL
Dr. Castellanos-Bright. I think I'd like some of that pain medicine after all.

IMELDA
(slowly)
Why's that, Mr. Wendell?

WENDELL
Because it's starting.

He looks down at his hands. They are going translucent, like wax over a flame.

TOOTS
(whispering)
Doc, back away.

Imelda doesn't. She reaches out and takes Wendell's hand, which is already cooling.

IMELDA
Toots, tell dispatch to cancel the ambulance.

TOOTS
Doc--

IMELDA
(not looking away)
Tell them he's been pronounced.

Toots stares at her. Then he lifts the radio, and his voice breaks.

TOOTS
(into radio)
Dispatch, Mobile Two. Cancel the ambulance.

WENDELL
Thank you for staying.

The sheet settles over an empty gurney. Outside, the carousel starts again from the beginning.
